  "assumptions": [
    "RDS default is Single-AZ db.m7g.large; source-class memory retained and no CPU credit charge.",
    "All Aurora profiles contain one writer and zero readers. A single writer has distributed durable storage but no warm compute failover reader.",
    "Cheap Aurora uses slow-statement logs and pg_stat_statements with basic CloudWatch metrics; Advanced/Performance Insights is reserved for the >=2-ACU profiles.",
    "Aurora warm floor is a cost floor, not evidence that Platform can run at that size. Current CPU, connections and cache can prevent scaling to the floor.",
    "Paused profile assumes no user connections or work; current persistent pools/background traffic prevent that condition without deliberate changes.",
    "App and active DB writer are pinned to the same AZ, use private addresses and have no NAT or cross-AZ data path in the base design.",
    "RDS subnet group still includes private subnets in two AZs; empty subnets alone do not create a second DB or gateway bill.",
    "t3a.xlarge alternative assumes zero surplus CPU credits. Validate 40% baseline and measure real credits before choosing it.",
    "RDS Multi-AZ SKU rates include the standby; the optional upgrade does not make the single app VM highly available.",
    "EBS and database backup budgets are assumed chargeable GiB-month beyond applicable free/included allowances.",
    "Existing GCP dev/shared DB, rollback hold, object stores, screener/validator compute, private trace sinks, inference providers and engineering labor remain outside this new AWS footprint."
  ]
